                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6374/1071: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-07T12:00:00-04:00">January 7,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. I believe the Chilean Government has a definite plan for procedure in the
                    liquidation of Cosach but it has made no official statement and has refused to
                    give any intimation to the company concerning it. It is of immediate importance
                    to American interests to know what changes in the capital structure are
                    contemplated. I suggest that, unless the Department perceives some objection, I
                    talk with the Minister of Finance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
